The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes and enhances its uptake by antigen-presenting cells. Figure 5a presents flow cytometry plots showing the detection and phenotyping of OVA-positive (OVA+) cells in the draining lymph nodes after injection of OVA alone or adjuvanted with aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 on day 1 and day 2. Figure 5b quantifies the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in these cells, demonstrating that Nano-11 significantly increases OVA uptake per cell compared to OVA alone or OVA+AH. Figure 5c indicates that Nano-11 also increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among the OVA-positive cell population.